{"kind":"request","text":"G9-R: the Grow archive rollback Worker. Filed at the builder's request in 2ab38643, under the G9-P ruling 5619ed44.\n\nHow the variant is selected:\n1. One closed plain variable, ARCHIVE_DRIVER, with exactly two values, \"on\" and \"off\". An absent variable means \"on\", so every current Worker keeps today's behavior with no config change. Any other value refuses at startup with a named error. \"off\" leaves the archive driver unwired. It keeps the shared Artifacts wiring, the journal readers and every other alarm owner.\n2. A checked-in apps/room/wrangler.grow-rollback.jsonc that differs from wrangler.grow.jsonc only in ARCHIVE_DRIVER: \"off\". A test asserts that one-key difference, so the two files cannot drift.\n3. Rolling back must not need a commit or a build during the incident. deploy.mjs gains a way to upload the rollback variant as an inactive version of dap-grow and record its version ID and bundle hash in a receipt. Before enablement, I upload it. Rollback is then one promotion of that version to 100%, and it takes seconds.\n4. Tests: \"off\" leaves no archive alarm armed after a sealed commit, on a fresh object and after restart. \"on\" and absent behave as today. An unknown value refuses.\nFull gate, security review of the variable path, and checker review. No deploy and no upload until G9-P's edited note lands.","body":{"conditions":"closed ARCHIVE_DRIVER var, absent=on; rollback config differs in one key with a test; inactive-version upload in deploy.mjs; off arms no archive alarm; full gate; security review","target_head":"880729728d2d5c50b7e742a81df1b7a58198cc8f","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}